---
description: New Blazor checkboxes and radios must be gray (not Bootstrap white) when unchecked
alwaysApply: true
---

# Unchecked checkboxes and radios are gray

Bootstrap draws an unchecked `form-check-input` white, which clashes with the dark theme. Whenever you add a new checkbox or radio button to a Blazor page, modal or component, give the input both classes:

```razor
<input class="form-check-input form-check-input-gray" type="checkbox" ... />
```

`.form-check-input-gray` (in `GrayMoon/src/GrayMoon.App/wwwroot/app.css`) sets the gray `--bg-input` background and `--border-light` border while unchecked; the checked state keeps the normal accent color. Do not add one-off per-page overrides for this. Switches (`role="switch"`) are already gray and do not need the class.

The same rule applies to WPF dialogs in GrayMoon.Desktop: use the dark `CheckBox` style (gray `#3e3e42` box) from `WorkerUpgradeDialog.xaml`, never the default white WPF checkbox.
